  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/b162564c1a2ba7f963986afb6ccbfc187769c9d04204e51dbed6afe9bcee976c.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above, where $\\overset{\\to }{SP}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=b,$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PT}=c.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{SQ}$ in terms of $a,b$ and $c.$",
  "worked_solution": "We want to find a \"path\" from $P$ to $Q$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,$ and $c.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{SQ}=\\overset{\\to }{SP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/821f008f5c77a2b632794077eca4da1405fe9dd77d1dd000176c5fba99a8fd98.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{SP}=a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=b.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/4fb266a59e1d2a8ec28c4f304d05b19aa678346e429f91669590f47e9c15c9da.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{SQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{SP}+\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =a+b\\end{aligned}\n$$",
